# 15. DATABASE ACCESS POLICIES

Create and verify Row Level Security policies.

Required access behaviour:

- Public visitors can read eligible public letters.
- Unlisted letters are not discoverable through public feeds or search.
- Unlisted letter content can be retrieved through a valid direct-link flow.
- Owners can read and modify their own letters.
- Owners cannot modify other people's letters.
- Users can create and manage their own replies.
- Users cannot modify other people's replies.
- Users can manage their own saved letters.
- Users can read their own notifications.
- Users cannot read other users' reports or moderation notes.
- Administrators have restricted, server-verified moderation access.
- No user can assign themselves an administrator role.

Do not rely on hiding buttons in the frontend as authorization.

Test RLS policies with different user roles.

Pay particular attention to anonymous Supabase users, which use the authenticated database role but have an anonymous identity claim.

